{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"**Landed.** Change 1706 submitted and merged as `5f4a5c1d40` (Gerrit rebased on submit, so the merged sha differs from the pushed `e3a97d57c5`). Worktree realigned to `gerrit/main`.\n\nAcceptance criteria verified against the **landed** tree:\n\n- AC1 PASS — `fsck.py` 301 lines (<= 400).\n- AC2 PASS — `fsck_scan.py` 387, `fsck_tracker_health.py` 235, both >= 100.\n- AC3 PASS — `pytest tests/unit/test_module_size_contract.py` 4 passed.\n- AC4 PASS — all six symbols resolve as `fsck.<attr>` (`_resolve_tracker_git_dir`, `foreign_store_path_list`, `_check_snapshot`, `_scan`, `_tracker_sync_status`, `_foreign_store_paths`).\n- AC5 PASS — `gitutil.py`, `fsck_recover.py`, `tracker_maintenance.py` untouched (no diff).\n- AC6 PASS — the landed commit's file list is exactly four entries, none under `tests/`.\n- AC7 PASS — 428 passed, 9 skipped across `tests/interfaces/store/` + the creation-channel compaction suite.\n- AC8/AC9 PASS — `make lint` and `make typecheck` green.\n- AC10 PASS — `check_complexity_baseline.py --lock` reports `OK (no raised ceilings or new entries)`; the full CI selection ran green pre-merge (12633 passed, 0 failed) and CI cast `Verified +1`.\n\nOne unrelated pre-existing failure was excluded from the AC7 run: `test_bridge_preview_under_sync_contention_heldout.py` fails with `ModuleNotFoundError: No module named 'rebar_reconciler'` — a stale venv in this worktree, reproduced identically at the parent commit `1c3e945cb8`. The landed commit touches zero reconciler files and CI passed on a pristine checkout.\n\nFollow-ons filed: `untameable-tweedy-wildebeast` (fsck's shared filesystem primitives live in the repair module, linked `discovered_from`); `bloated-shadeful-lamprey` already covers `_lib_writes.py`, which has since reached the cap itself."},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1786605120081470001,"uuid":"f6c92b30-7ecc-4c71-8087-7217ded2dbf9"}